# Logging & Tracing

## Logger API

```typescript
import { logger, createLogger } from "~/shared/lib/logger";

// Global logger
logger.info("App started", { runtime: "browser" });
logger.error("Failed to connect", { status: 503 });

// Scoped logger
const apiLog = createLogger("api");
apiLog.warn("Slow response", { ms: 3200, endpoint: "/messages" });

// Child logger
const chatLog = logger.child("chat");
chatLog.info("Message sent", { streamId: 5, topic: "general" });
```

## Log Levels

| Level | When | Production |
|-------|------|------------|
| `debug` | Development tracing, state changes | Suppressed |
| `info` | Significant events (login, connect, navigate) | Suppressed |
| `warn` | Recoverable problems (slow API, retry) | Logged |
| `error` | Failures (API error, uncaught exception) | Logged |

Default min level: `debug` (dev), `warn` (production).

## Security: NEVER log these

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER
logger.info("Login", { apiKey: instance.apiKey });
logger.error("Auth failed", { password: input.value });
logger.debug("Request", { headers: { Authorization: authHeader } });

// ✅ SAFE (auto-redacted, but still — avoid passing secrets)
logger.info("Login", { realm: instance.realm, email: instance.email });
logger.error("Auth failed", { status: 401, realm: "zulip.example.com" });
logger.debug("Request", { method: "GET", path: "/api/v1/messages" });
```

Auto-redaction catches keys like `apiKey`, `password`, `token`, `authorization`, `secret`, `csrf`, `session` and values matching Basic/Bearer auth patterns. But **prevention is better than sanitization** — don't pass secrets to the logger at all.

## Helper Functions

```typescript
import { logApiCall, logEvent, logStoreAction } from "~/shared/lib/logger";

// API call tracing
logApiCall("GET", "/messages", { status: 200, durationMs: 150 });
logApiCall("POST", "/messages", { error: "Network error" });

// Real-time event tracing
logEvent("message", { messageId: 123, type: "stream" });

// Store action tracing
logStoreAction("chatList", "addMessage", { messageId: 123 });
```

## Log History (Debug UI)

```typescript
import { getLogHistory, clearLogHistory } from "~/shared/lib/logger";

const entries = getLogHistory(); // Last 500 entries (ring buffer)
clearLogHistory();
```

Use for in-app debug screens and developer diagnostics surfaces.

## Sentry Integration

When `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` is present:
- Logger error/warn → Sentry breadcrumbs (automatically via transport)
- ErrorBoundary → `captureException()` (automatically)
- Unhandled rejections → Sentry (automatically)

Manual capture:
```typescript
import { captureException, captureMessage, setUser, clearUser } from "~/shared/lib/sentry";

captureException(error, { context: "custom info" });
captureMessage("Something happened", "warning");
setUser(userId, email);   // after login
clearUser();              // after logout
```

## Custom Transports

```typescript
import { addTransport, type LogTransport } from "~/shared/lib/logger";

const remoteTransport: LogTransport = {
  write(entry) {
    if (entry.level === "error") {
      fetch("/api/logs", {
        method: "POST",
        body: JSON.stringify(entry),
      }).catch(() => {});
    }
  },
};
addTransport(remoteTransport);
```

## Where to Log

| Location | Logger scope | What to log |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| API client (`shared/api/client.ts`) | `api` | Requests, responses (status+duration), errors |
| Event loop (`app/app.event-loop.ts`) | `realtime` | Queue registration, events received, reconnects |
| Stores | `store:<name>` | State changes, action calls |
| Components | `ui:<name>` | User interactions (sparingly) |
| Auth flow | `auth` | Login/logout events (NO credentials) |
| Error boundaries | `error` | Uncaught exceptions with stack |

## Rules for AI Agent

When adding new code:
1. Use `createLogger("scope")` — never raw `console.log/warn/error`
2. Always use structured data: `logger.info("msg", { key: value })` — not string interpolation
3. Never pass user credentials, API keys, or tokens to log data
4. For API calls, log method + path + status + duration — never log request/response bodies
5. For real-time events, log event type + minimal identifiers — never log message content
